Pseudocode, direkt nutzbar) -- Polynom als Liste von
Koeffizienten a0 + a1 x + a2 x\^2 + ... type Coeffs a = \[a\] --
Horner-Evaluator (semantics parametrisierbar) evalHorner :: Num a =\>
Coeffs a -\> a -\> a evalHorner coeffs x = foldr (`\c a`{=tex}cc -\> c +
x * acc) 0 (reverse coeffs) -- Transformations (delegierende
Komposition) mapCoeffs :: (a -\> b) -\> Coeffs a -\> Coeffs b mapCoeffs
= map composePolys :: Num a =\> Coeffs a -\> Coeffs a -\> Coeffs a --
